                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Spelunky is a drug, the kind of drug that really harms your mental health... The game design is devilishly good: a roguelike platformer with simple controls, with bombs and ropes in limited amount to help you. But behind the apparent simplicity, everything can be a trap. The game does an excellent job at making the player think he can go through levels quickly and easily although he's actually in constant danger and death is lurking at every corner. This makes the game both cynical and addictive, as you're always tempted to think your last death was not meant to happen. \n\nIf you're stubborn enough to go far in the game, you'll be rewarded with a lot to discover: levels, mobs, objects, and a lot of secrets. There is also a roguelite mechanic allowing you to unlock the possibility to start at later stages of the game, although you will likely quickly realize - at least I did - that your best chance of finishing the game is still to start from the very first level. Last good point to mention: a nice OST with 16-bit vibes. \n\nThis game made me angry many times, and still I can't help loving it. Wonderfully crafted with excellent game design.",
